nd  investigates he eventually comes across  her handmaidens and her handmaidens  believe that both anakin and padme were  killed by darth vader so  almost no one really seems to know that  vader and anakin are the same person so  i find that a little strange and even if  it is one of those things where by some  mystery she somehow knows i don't really  know how i feel about that because i  love the idea that anakin and vader  being the same person but this being  like a ridiculously well-kept secret one  that's that's so well kept that those  who learn about it would actually end up  being killed i i really love that idea  right i really love that that whole  thing again there's nothing being taken  away from the show by this right it's  not as though the show is somehow  diminished because riva knows that  anakin is darth vader but you know it's  just something that just doesn't quite  it kind of rubs me the wrong way having  said that i do love that we got to see  vader in that moment you know once once  i was about maybe a quarter of the way  through episode two i was like okay  we're not going to see vader in this  episode given everything that's  happening and how it's transpiring we're  not really going to see like darth vader  showing up in all his glory in this  episode that's not really gonna happen  if anything it'll end up just being a a  scene at the very end of the show and  then of course that turned out to be the  case  i think this is a good move i think it's  a great decision on behalf of disney in  them because if if they had if they had  shown their hand too early right if they  had if they had revealed their hand too  early it would have taken away from this  suspense because we're all kind of  waiting for that duel between anakin and  darth vader which as i understand is  supposed to happen in the show you know  i'm i'm excited to see that and i think  most everybody's excited to see that too  and kind of prolonging that and kind of  allowing things to build up seems pretty  cool but again i think a lot of that  goes back to the nature of riva and the  fact that they're focusing very heavily  on her character and presumably the the  vendetta or the grudge that she holds  against obi-wan kenobi that goes deeper  than her just trying to work her way up  the ranks of the sith to  you know maybe the second in command to  darth vader right or the first in  command of darth vader or whatever the  case happens to be right it's his right  hand so to speak again we don't fully  know what her motivations are i am  excited to find out that being said  again you know the first two episodes  like largely feel like filler episodes  it seems like a lot of stuff that  happened in this in the first two  episodes just wasn't really necessary it  felt like they were just kind of killing  time finding a reason to create six  episodes i think there are other things  they could have done in here besides  focusing on that one of the things that  i would have loved to have seen that i  thought would have been very very  fascinating here is to show us what  obi-wan kenobi was doing between the end  of episode three and this right like we  know that obi-wan kenobi took the kids  to tatooine and he dropped the kids off  and that basically seemed to be it but i  would like to have believed that there  was a little more going on to obi-wan  kenobi than that that even if we don't  necessarily see that at the very least  you know whether he was using the force  or what have you we get a glimpse into  what else was happening we get that  momentarily right like literally when  those those those clones come running in  guns blazing and just mow down everybody  right i mean you know i guess i  shouldn't laugh at that but like i mean  we kind of get that moment right and  those young links take off and it's like  we run it's like well you're gonna die  because like ob like literally anakin's  gonna come in there and kill all of you  so you 