 normal person and rightfully so  because they are  but when you you know if you if you look  at the the video game kotor 2 right star  wars ice cream republic 2. there's a  really good point where the character  treya by the way spoiler for a 15  20 year old game there's a point where  where crea who turns out to be a sith  lord is actually talking to the exile  right the main character of the game and  she's saying that if you take the force  and lightsabers away from the jedi then  what are they right they're nothing more  than the weakest people you've ever seen  fumbling around with like a blaster or  something like that with this i think it  shows us just how capable obi-wan kenobi  is that even in utilizing the force only  really once in any real measure when he  you know keeps uh keeps leia from  falling to the ground he's still able to  pull things off right he's still able to  use espionage subterfuge it's obvious  he's a bit rusty right with his fighting  style i mean it looked a little rough  and i like how they played into it right  i mean obviously ewan mcgregor is not as  young as he was when he was doing  episodes one two and three so there's  there's the real life age factor that  goes into that he can't quite move the  same way i love that they leaned into  that where he's like it's been 10 years  i'm not the jedi i used to be you know  i'm rusty man you know and i'm not as  capable i love that they built that in  because that goes strongly towards  obi-wan kenobi and episode four and that  was one of the big things that i was  always curious about that you saw  obi-wan kenobi in episode three with  just this extravagant and albeit amazing  lightsaber duel with anakin and it's  like how do we go from that obi-wan  kenobi to like old man ben who obviously  is not fighting anywhere near the same  capacity when he faced off against vader  in episode four and so it's like how do  you how do you get to that is it really  just age like does a jedi's ability to  utilize the force really just diminish  with age or does it diminish with a lack  of use right is it like a muscle it just  atrophies after a while and what this  really looks like is the longer a jedi  goes without using the force and the  skills that it that it allows  they really do just become weaker as  time goes on they become less capable  and i loved that i love that they gave  us an obi-wan kenobi that really just  had to rely on his wits and his  capabilities his fortitudes absent any  real use of the force i think it really  showcases just how capable obi-wan  kenobi is as a character as opposed to  like he's a jedi master who can do  anything because he's got the force and  he can just jedi mind trick everybody  and call it a day and rescue princess  leia in like an hour and a half but i  mean it's it's cool to see him you know  literally use a blaster when he's  running up on what's his name the fake  jedi which was a hilarious moment um  again you know i think that this this  really showcased how awesome he is as  just a capable person more so than just  a guy who needs the force and able to  pull anything off but again nothing in  the show is bad it was not really  disappointing i i didn't walk away from  it saying like man this kind of sucks  you know it was cool and in a lot of  ways it was what i was expecting given  the disney shows that we've seen so far  mandalorian was a very slow burn boba  fett was actually it was slow to its own  detriment  you know so i expected this to be much  the same way it really seems to be the  formula that disney's following in  relation to like their their star wars  franchises i i will say i do think the  first two episodes are going to be very  divisive and i think there's going to be  a lot of people out there who absolutely  thought they were great and a lot of  people who were just like this was  boring and it sucks right i feel like  this that's really going to be where  things split but at the end of the day  like so many shows that come out now  especially when you're only talking  about six episodes right like six weeks  a month and a half i think it is  necessary to sit down and let the show  run its course and to see where the show  leads and just kind of allow us to see  it go to its conclusion because i think  in a lot of ways it could feel very much  like loki where loki was slow in a lot  of ways in the beginning there were some  action sequences but there were times  when i was in the show and i was like  okay so like where's this going you know  and then you get to like the last two  episodes and it's like holy cow right  like one division was the same way one  division just kind of snaked along for  the first two episodes lost a lot of  people and then by the time you started  getting halfway through the show you're  like okay things are kind of picking up  you get to the end you're like holy hell  right so you know i really have a  feeling that obi-wan is going to feel  much the same way so uh with that being  said guys let me know what you think  down in the comments right were you a  huge fan of it were you just kind of  like  this is it's okay you know it's a thing  that exists let me know what you guys  think thank you all for watching i will  catch you all later  peace
 

